# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jianxing Huang et al. (2021). Deep potential generation scheme and simulation protocol for the Li10GeP2S12-type superionic conductors.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0041849  arXiv:2006.03320v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2006.03320v3 (sha256 b120b6e0dff46ee2...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 606 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/huang2021.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the DP-PBE and DP-PBEsol Deep Potential models (DeePMD
# v1.2, DP-GEN) for Li10GeP2S12, Li10SiP2S12 and Li10SnP2S12, with the
# per-material RMSEs on the whole DP-GEN data set (Table V, mean of a
# 4-model ensemble). Diffusion coefficients, lattice parameters and
# thermal expansion are property results.

