###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table V errors are on the whole DP-GEN data set (no held-out split is described), so they are encoded with role training; the ensemble standard deviations (e.g. +/-0.03 meV/atom) are not encoded.
# - The speed test (Fig. 6) is given only approximately ('around 4 hours' for 1 ns of a 900-atom system on one V100) and is not encoded. The data-set size is not stated.
# - Diffusion coefficients, activation energies, lattice parameters (Table II, DFT only) and thermal expansion are property results and are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/huang2021.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

